---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { BROKER } from '../config/site';
---

<Base
  title="About Jordan Buttarazzi, Broker"
  description="Jordan Buttarazzi, Broker with Valery Real Estate Inc., Brokerage. RECO #5009855. Buyer representation for new freehold low-rise across the GTA: detached homes, townhomes and semis."
  kicker={['Ontario', 'Low-rise', 'About']}
  width="narrow"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About', href: '/about' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6">
    <p class="section-label">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-[2rem] font-semibold sm:text-[2.6rem]">
      {BROKER.name}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[16px] text-ink/60">{BROKER.title}, {BROKER.brokerage}</p>

    <p class="lede mt-7">
      I represent buyers of new freehold low-rise across the GTA. Detached homes, townhomes and
      semis. Not condos.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85">
      <p>
        Most pre-construction advice is written about condominiums, because that is where the
        marketing budgets are. Low-rise is a different transaction. The agreement is firmer, the
        deposit protection is thinner, the closing costs are higher, and the purchase is usually
        larger. Nobody writes about it properly, so I did.
      </p>
      <p>
        What I actually do is unglamorous and it is where the money is. I read the agreement
        alongside your lawyer and tell you what the HST clause really commits you to. I tell you
        which builders hit their dates and which do not, because that is not on any price list. I
        tell you which lot premiums hold their value and which are three feet of grass. And I tell
        you when a release is not worth your time.
      </p>
      <p>
        The builder budgets a co-operating commission into the price whether or not you bring a
        broker. Walk into a sales centre alone and they keep it. The price does not drop. So the
        real choice is not whether to pay for representation. It is whether to have someone in the
        room whose obligation is to you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-rule pt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What I am not</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85">
        A lawyer, an accountant or a mortgage agent. The rebate content on this site explains
        published CRA and Tarion rules and cites its sources so you can check them. When a question
        turns on the law or on your tax position, I will tell you to take it to the right person.
        On a rebate worth up to $80,000, that is the only responsible answer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-rule pt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Registration</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-[15px]">
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <dt class="w-28 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Brokerage</dt>
          <dd class="font-medium text-ink">{BROKER.brokerage}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <dt class="w-28 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Registrant</dt>
          <dd class="text-ink">{BROKER.name}, {BROKER.title}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <dt class="w-28 shrink-0 text-ink/55">RECO</dt>
          <dd class="figure text-ink">#{BROKER.reco}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <dt class="w-28 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Phone</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href={BROKER.phoneHref} class="figure text-accent underline underline-offset-2">
              {BROKER.phone}
            </a>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <dt class="w-28 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Email</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href={`mailto:${BROKER.email}`} class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">
              {BROKER.email}
            </a>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <dt class="w-28 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Serves</dt>
          <dd class="text-ink/80">{BROKER.areaServed}</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[13px] text-ink/55">
        Full terms on which this information is provided are on the
        <a href="/disclaimer" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">disclaimer page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <Cta variant="vip" heading="Buying new low-rise?" />
  </div>
</Base>
